from dbhelp import *
AHF=dis("ahf","Acute heart failure",
["Early acute heart failure. At organ level, the patient is breathless and the legs swell. At cellular level, heart muscle cells contract with less force and pressure rises behind the ventricle.",
 "Established acute heart failure. At organ level, the lungs congest and the kidneys receive less flow. At cellular level, neurohormones hold salt and water and add load to the failing cells.",
 "Severe acute heart failure. At organ level, fluid floods the alveoli and organ perfusion falls. At cellular level, myocytes are short of energy and calcium handling fails.",
 "Critical acute heart failure. At organ level, cardiogenic shock appears with cold limbs and low blood pressure. At cellular level, myocyte death and microcirculatory failure drive a downward spiral."],
"Decongest and perfuse","Decongest and perfuse. Vasodilators and diuretics relieve the lungs, and inotropes or mechanical support restore flow when output is low.",
[["pe","cs","Rising pressure and falling output feed each other"],["cs","aki","Low output cuts kidney perfusion"],["aki","pe","Failing kidneys retain volume and flood the lungs"]],
[
comp("pe",["Pulmonary","edema"],-90,.2,{"a":"alveolus"},
 {"fluid":[0,.9],"stretch":[0,.1],"inflam":[0,.05],"vent":[.5,.5]},
 [["SpO2","fluid",98,76,"%","<",92,0],["Wedge pressure","fluid",8,35,"mmHg",">",18,0]],
 [rx("niv","Non invasive ventilation",H,"recruits flooded alveoli and lowers preload",fluid=-.25),
  rx("loop","IV loop diuretic",H,"promotes salt and water loss",fluid=-.3),
  rx("nitr","Nitrates",H,"dilate veins and lower filling pressure",fluid=-.3),
  rx("morph","Morphine",X,"respiratory depression leads to more intubation",vent=-.2,fluid=.1),
  rx("ivf","IV fluid bolus",X,"raises capillary pressure",fluid=.3),
  rx("bb","Beta blocker in acute pulmonary edema",X,"further depresses a failing ventricle",fluid=.15)],
 "Acute myocardial infarction, arrhythmia, hypertensive crisis, acute mitral regurgitation and fluid overload.",
 "Often rapidly reversible with decongestion and afterload reduction.",
 "Pulmonary edema, organ level. The failing left ventricle cannot empty, so pressure backs up into the lungs. The patient is breathless and may cough pink frothy sputum.",
 "Pulmonary edema, cell level. High pressure in the lung capillaries forces fluid across the thin wall and breaks it. The alveoli fill and gas exchange falls.",
 ["Early. At organ level, the patient is breathless on exertion. At cellular level, pressure rises in the lung capillaries.",
  "Interstitial edema. At organ level, the patient is breathless at rest. At cellular level, fluid collects around the alveoli.",
  "Alveolar edema. At organ level, crackles are heard and oxygen falls. At cellular level, fluid pours into the air sacs.",
  "Severe. At organ level, the patient is drowning in frothy fluid. At cellular level, the alveolar barrier has failed."]),
comp("cs",["Cardiogenic","shock"],30,.4,{"a":"heart"},
 {"con":[1,-.8],"lvdil":[0,.6],"rate":[.3,.5],"congest":[0,.5],"rvf":[1,-.2],"sept":[0,.1]},
 [["Cardiac index","con",.8,2.8,"L/min/m²","<",2.2,1],["Systolic pressure","con",60,125,"mmHg","<",90,0]],
 [rx("revasc","Revascularisation",H,"reopens the culprit artery",con=.35),
  rx("nor","Noradrenaline",H,"supports pressure and coronary perfusion",con=.1),
  rx("dobu","Dobutamine",H,"raises contractility but adds tachycardia",con=.25,rate=.1),
  rx("mcs","Mechanical circulatory support",H,"takes over part of the pumping",con=.35,lvdil=-.2),
  rx("bb","Beta blocker",X,"further depresses the failing pump",con=-.25,rate=-.15),
  rx("fluid","Large fluid bolus",X,"overfills a failing ventricle",lvdil=.2,congest=.2)],
 "Large myocardial infarction, myocarditis, mechanical complications such as acute valve failure or septal rupture, and arrhythmia.",
 "Reversible only if the cause, such as an occluded artery, is corrected quickly. Delay leads to multi organ failure.",
 "Cardiogenic shock, organ level. The ventricle cannot pump enough blood. Pressure falls, the skin turns cold, and the kidneys, liver and brain lose perfusion.",
 "Cardiogenic shock, cell level. Myocytes lack energy and calcium handling fails, so contraction weakens. Inflammatory signals and nitric oxide dilate vessels and deepen the shock.",
 ["Early. At organ level, blood pressure is borderline. At cellular level, ischaemic muscle contracts with less force.",
  "Low output. At organ level, the pulse rate rises and the limbs are cool. At cellular level, calcium handling begins to fail.",
  "Shock. At organ level, pressure and urine output fall. At cellular level, muscle cells run out of energy.",
  "Refractory shock. At organ level, several organs fail. At cellular level, myocytes die and the microcirculation collapses."]),
comp("aki",["AKI"],150,.35,{"a":"nephron"},
 {"gfr":[1,-.65],"injury":[0,.55],"urea":[0,.5],"k":[0,.4],"acid":[0,.35]},
 [["Creatinine","injury",.9,3.5,"mg/dL",">",1.5,1],["Urine output","gfr",0,60,"ml/h","<",30,0]],
 [rx("co","Restore cardiac output",H,"restores renal perfusion",gfr=.3,injury=-.2),
  rx("dec","Decongestion with diuretic",H,"lowers renal venous pressure",gfr=.15),
  rx("noN","Avoid nephrotoxins",H,"removes extra insults",injury=-.1),
  rx("rrt","Renal replacement therapy",H,"removes solutes and fluid",urea=-.4,k=-.3,acid=-.3),
  rx("acei","ACE inhibitor in shock",X,"lowers filtration pressure and raises potassium",gfr=-.2,k=.15),
  rx("nsaid","NSAIDs",X,"lower renal blood flow",gfr=-.15,injury=.2)],
 "Low cardiac output, venous congestion, nephrotoxic drugs and contrast.",
 "Usually reversible if the heart recovers; persistent low output causes tubular necrosis.",
 "Cardiorenal AKI, organ level. Low output cuts kidney blood flow, while venous congestion raises back pressure in the renal veins. Both lower filtration.",
 "Cardiorenal AKI, cell level. Tubule cells are short of oxygen under low flow and congestion. Neurohormonal activation adds vasoconstriction and sodium retention.",
 ["Early. At organ level, urine output is falling. At cellular level, tubule cells are short of oxygen.",
  "Mild. At organ level, creatinine begins to rise. At cellular level, venous congestion lowers filtration pressure.",
  "Moderate. At organ level, the patient retains salt and water. At cellular level, tubule cells begin to detach.",
  "Severe. At organ level, the patient is oliguric with potassium and acid build up. At cellular level, tubule cells are dying."]),
])

TBI=dis("tbi","Traumatic brain injury",
["Early TBI. At organ level, the patient has a depressed conscious level after impact. At cellular level, the primary injury has torn axons and opened cell membranes.",
 "Established TBI. At organ level, swelling and bleeding begin. At cellular level, glutamate and calcium flood the neurons and mitochondria fail.",
 "Severe TBI. At organ level, intracranial pressure rises and perfusion falls. At cellular level, cells swell, so more volume squeezes the brain.",
 "Critical TBI. At organ level, the brain herniates and the pupils dilate. At cellular level, ischaemia and swelling kill neurons and brainstem function."],
"Neuroprotective care","Neuroprotective care. Head up, normal oxygen, carbon dioxide and sodium, adequate perfusion pressure, and osmotherapy or surgery for pressure.",
[["icp","hern","Rising pressure pushes brain through the tentorium"],["icp","isch","High pressure cuts perfusion"],["hern","isch","Compression of vessels deepens ischaemia"]],
[
comp("icp",["Raised","ICP"],-90,.3,{"a":"brain"},
 {"swell":[0,.7],"mass":[0,.5],"shift":[0,.35],"perf":[1,-.5],"isch":[0,.3],"hern":[0,.15]},
 [["ICP","swell",10,40,"mmHg",">",22,0],["CPP","perf",30,90,"mmHg","<",60,0]],
 [rx("head","Head up 30 degrees",H,"improves venous drainage",swell=-.1),
  rx("hts","Hypertonic saline",H,"draws water out of the brain",swell=-.25),
  rx("mann","Mannitol",H,"osmotic reduction of brain volume",swell=-.2),
  rx("evd","CSF drainage (EVD)",H,"removes fluid from the skull",swell=-.2),
  rx("surg","Evacuation of a mass lesion",H,"removes the space occupying clot",mass=-.4,shift=-.3),
  rx("hypo","Hypotonic fluids",X,"water moves into the injured brain",swell=.25),
  rx("hypot","Hypotension or hypoxia",X,"cuts brain perfusion",perf=-.3,isch=.2),
  rx("hv","Prolonged hyperventilation",X,"constricts brain vessels",perf=-.2,isch=.2)],
 "Haematoma, contusion, diffuse swelling, hydrocephalus, hypoventilation, seizures and fever.",
 "Reversible early with osmotherapy, drainage or surgery. Prolonged high pressure causes permanent ischaemic injury.",
 "Raised ICP, organ level. The skull is a rigid box. Bleeding or swelling adds volume, pressure rises, and blood flow into the brain falls.",
 "Raised ICP, cell level. Injured neurons and astrocytes swell and endothelial cells leak, adding water to the brain. Cells that lose blood supply swell further.",
 ["Early. At organ level, the intracranial pressure is normal. At cellular level, injured cells begin to swell.",
  "Mild. At organ level, pressure is creeping up. At cellular level, the blood brain barrier starts to leak.",
  "Moderate. At organ level, ventricles are squeezed and perfusion falls. At cellular level, cells swell and add volume.",
  "Severe. At organ level, pressure is high and the midline shifts. At cellular level, ischaemia and swelling feed each other."]),
comp("hern",["Hernia-","tion"],30,.5,{"a":"brain"},
 {"hern":[0,.95],"shift":[0,.8],"swell":[0,.8],"mass":[0,.6],"perf":[1,-.7],"isch":[0,.5]},
 [["Pupil","hern",3,8,"mm",">",5,0],["GCS","hern",15,3,"","<",8,0]],
 [rx("hyper","Hyperosmolar bolus",H,"rapidly shrinks brain volume",hern=-.3,swell=-.2),
  rx("hv","Brief hyperventilation as a bridge",H,"rapidly lowers pressure",hern=-.15,swell=-.1),
  rx("crani","Emergency craniectomy or evacuation",H,"gives the brain room",hern=-.4,mass=-.4,shift=-.3),
  rx("head","Head up, avoid neck compression",H,"helps venous drainage",swell=-.05),
  rx("lp","Lumbar puncture",X,"can cause coning when pressure is high",hern=.3),
  rx("hypo","Hypotonic fluids",X,"raise brain volume",swell=.2,hern=.1)],
 "Large mass lesion, severe diffuse swelling, uncontrolled pressure and delayed treatment.",
 "Time critical. Early reversal can recover the patient; established brainstem compression is usually fatal or severely disabling.",
 "Herniation, organ level. The brain is pushed across the midline and down through the tentorium. The pupil dilates, the patient becomes comatose, and breathing and blood pressure change.",
 "Herniation, cell level. Displaced tissue compresses brainstem neurons and the vessels that supply them. Axons stretch and shear, and ischaemia stops their function.",
 ["Early. At organ level, the patient has headache and drowsiness. At cellular level, pressure compresses nearby tissue.",
  "Midline shift. At organ level, the brain shifts across the midline. At cellular level, axons stretch and the ventricles squeeze.",
  "Uncal herniation. At organ level, the pupil dilates and the patient is drowsy. At cellular level, the oculomotor nerve is compressed.",
  "Brainstem compression. At organ level, the patient is comatose with abnormal breathing. At cellular level, brainstem neurons are squeezed and ischaemic."]),
comp("isch",["Ischemia"],150,.35,{"a":"brain"},
 {"perf":[1,-.85],"isch":[0,.95],"swell":[0,.45],"hern":[0,.1],"mass":[0,.2]},
 [["Brain oxygen (PbtO2)","perf",5,35,"mmHg","<",20,0],["CPP","perf",30,90,"mmHg","<",60,0]],
 [rx("cpp","Maintain CPP above 60",H,"restores brain blood flow",perf=.3,isch=-.2),
  rx("ox","Normal oxygen and carbon dioxide",H,"avoids hypoxia and vasoconstriction",isch=-.15),
  rx("bp","Avoid hypotension",H,"protects perfusion pressure",perf=.15),
  rx("fever","Avoid fever",H,"lowers metabolic demand",isch=-.05),
  rx("hypot","Hypotension",X,"cuts brain perfusion",perf=-.3,isch=.25),
  rx("hv","Hyperventilation",X,"constricts brain vessels",perf=-.2,isch=.2)],
 "Raised ICP with low blood pressure, hypoxia, vasospasm, hyperventilation and microvascular thrombosis.",
 "Reversible for a short time because of the penumbra, but sustained ischaemia produces infarction.",
 "Ischaemia, organ level. Pressure from swelling or low blood pressure reduces blood flow to injured brain. Regions around the injury starve and die.",
 "Ischaemia, cell level. Neurons run out of oxygen and glucose, pumps fail, calcium floods in, and excitotoxic glutamate kills nearby cells.",
 ["Early. At organ level, flow is a little low in injured areas. At cellular level, neurons switch to anaerobic metabolism.",
  "Penumbra. At organ level, tissue around the injury is at risk. At cellular level, cells keep their pumps running but have no reserve.",
  "Infarction begins. At organ level, areas of the brain stop working. At cellular level, pumps fail and calcium floods in.",
  "Severe. At organ level, large areas are infarcted. At cellular level, excitotoxic glutamate spreads injury to neighbours."]),
])
